WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.740
(gentle guitar music)
(birds chirping)

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.600
- Foster care really helped me

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.030
to see that there's so many
other people in the world

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:09.870
who don't have what everybody else has.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.790
- So what we try to do during this season

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.520
is see what are some ways
that we can do something

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.810
to lift someone up who's
going through a tough time.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:20.840
- I'm Nico Tortorella.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.610
I'm an actor, an activist
and a firm believer

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.530
that our differences
actually make us stronger.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:29.100
I'm on a journey with
IKEA, to meet real people

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:32.300
and discover the diverse
and spectacular ways

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.938
they celebrate the holidays.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:39.230
Maybe you celebrate on just one day,

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:41.050
enjoying time with your family.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:43.220
Or maybe you celebrate
throughout the entire month

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.230
and spend that family time helping others,

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.600
like the Berry family here in Indiana.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.860
- I'm Mike Berry.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:50.950
- And I'm Kristin Berry.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:51.880
- We're both authors,

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.980
and we also are bloggers and podcasters.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:57.508
All eight of our children were adopted.

00:00:57.508 --> 00:00:58.940
There are 10 of us, total.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.580
We have three grandchildren,

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:04.270
and we also have two son-in-laws, so 15.

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:06.184
We are an all-American family.

00:01:06.184 --> 00:01:07.920
(gentle guitar music)

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.560
- The Berry family consists
of a group of people

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.320
from all different walks of life.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:16.523
And this farm really is a place
to come together and heal.

00:01:16.523 --> 00:01:19.070
(upbeat guitar music)

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:21.040
Tell me a little bit about this farm.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.140
- Oh man, this farm, is, it's our oasis.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:25.670
It's perfect for a family like ours,

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:28.210
because it's out in the middle of nowhere.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:30.850
It's been a really good
sanctuary for our family.

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:34.030
We have six children living
at home, very active.

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:36.890
They have big imaginations, love adventure

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:39.890
and we recognized that our
children just needed space.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:41.510
We really wanted to give them a place

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:44.331
where they could just
make lasting memories.

00:01:44.331 --> 00:01:45.910
(donkey snorting)

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:48.140
- There's really something
very soothing and healing

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.810
about being around animals.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.050
So for our kids, the
connection with the animals

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:56.593
that we can have out here is priceless.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.010
(gentle music)

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:01.750
- We all come from different backgrounds

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:02.970
and different families,

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:06.690
and so this season can
really be triggering.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:09.780
One of the things that we
do is celebrate Advent.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.330
It takes the focus off of this one day

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.330
that can bring so much
anxiety and anticipation,

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:19.350
and excitement, but it
can sometimes be too much.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.560
By breaking up those four weeks before,

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.970
we can really celebrate the whole season

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:25.516
in a more relaxed way.

00:02:25.516 --> 00:02:27.060
(gentle guitar music)

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.780
- I'm beyond impressed with this family;

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:32.340
every December they find time to create

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.190
these care packages for other families.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:37.990
- Throughout our life as a
foster and adoptive family,

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:40.110
people have given us things.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:43.500
We really became aware of how it feels

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.440
to have somebody support us
during those tough times.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.490
And so one aspect that we wanted to draw

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:51.120
into our celebration of the holidays

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.430
is giving to others, but giving to others

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:56.490
in a way that brings respect and dignity.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.557
- When you're pulled from your home

00:02:58.557 --> 00:03:01.452
and placed in a home with
people you don't know,

00:03:01.452 --> 00:03:03.670
it can feel like a loss of identity.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:06.640
This care package can
bring a sense of normalcy

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.180
and a sense of together.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.150
- They're creating real memories

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:13.148
and hopefully some of those can
be really positive memories.

00:03:13.681 --> 00:03:16.430
- The holidays are not just
about our nuclear family;

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:18.750
it's about giving outside of ourselves.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.110
That's what they wanna leave behind

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:22.040
with these care packages.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.890
- What's everyone's favorite
part about this tradition?

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.133
- Doing something nice for other people.

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:28.775
- Makes me feel happy.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:30.550
- We were all part of
the foster care system,

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:31.840
so it feels good to give it to people

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:34.450
who are, like, going through
what we used to go through.

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:35.970
- We're gonna teach him that Santa's more

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.942
than just a person, that it's
something that anybody can be.

00:03:38.942 --> 00:03:40.450
- Santa lives kind of in all of us,

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.660
it's just up to us to tap into it.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.090
That's beautiful.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:47.890
- Christmas is something
bigger than just ourselves.

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:50.160
And our hope is that
our children carry that

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.030
into their adult lives.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.380
That when they look
back on their childhood,

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.730
of course, they remember the gifts,

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:57.100
and of course they remember the excitement

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:58.100
of Christmas morning.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.250
But that they also look back and remember

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:03.904
that they were able to give
to somebody who was in need.

00:04:03.904 --> 00:04:06.487
(emotional music)

00:04:08.786 --> 00:04:10.487
- I may never leave Berry's.

00:04:10.487 --> 00:04:12.239
Eight kids just turned into nine.

00:04:12.239 --> 00:04:14.135
I love you.
(bees buzzing)

